    "difficulty_reason": "After standard Mackey/Frobenius reciprocity, Littlewood–Richardson and Young-rule foundations, the selected recursion still requires a new skew restriction calculation for wreath-product induced characters, including the double-coset/sign decomposition and its extension from one-row to arbitrary outer partitions. The complete author Lemmas5.8–5.14 and TheoremB operator construction remain obligations, not assumed background; the signed induction and hook-skew-character cancellation must then produce the full alternating recursion with the m=1 and m-at-least2 cases. This new character-operator construction and its general recursive consequence are retained as one unit, with no separate helper or unrelated Sylow count.",
    "source_scope_note": "Exact Theorem5.1 restatement of TheoremA, with all stated m/n/k, lambda-partition, output-length and skew conventions. Native126–339/628–676/754–1082 retain standard context, authored k0 context, exact primary and every new supporting/continued proof. Exactly5 outside-scope reference-index substitutions, all primary/core spans byte-exact. Root-approved literal1020m versus1013/1022m−1,1065T_w inflation,869predicate and conjugate-indexedclosing remain unchanged beside complete author contexts; no formula/domain/conjugation repair. Native standard Mackey phi_g spelling differs from printed phi superscriptg, both literal definitions retained through source evidence. Exact73 triv aliases use the strict1-only pinned installed Noto renderer, with actual normal/script sizes and all neighbor checks; original serif/sans differences disclosed. Final3 actual passes are stable and all ref/glyph/overfull checks pass, but24 original math-mode tiny sizing warnings remain explicitly preserved. No warning suppression or unknown-face fallback. Unrelated Sylow outcomes excluded.",
